# Architecture (layered, keep it lean)

Keep code in these layers. Do not collapse domain logic into CSV I/O or `main`.

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| Domain | `src/domain/` | Pure models + aggregates (counts, `"Unknown"`). No I/O. |
| Reports | `src/reports/` | Use cases that build the two report row sets. |
| IO | `src/io/` | CSV read/write via stdlib `csv` only. |
| Main | `src/main.py` | Wire paths and call use cases. |

## Rules

- Prefer **composition** and pure functions over inheritance and frameworks.
- Ports/adapters: swap input source (full CSV vs filtered list) without changing domain.
- No database, no DI container, no Factory/Singleton/Observer unless clearly justified.
- Never overwrite input CSVs; write to `output/` with distinct names:
  - `legislators-support-oppose-count.csv`
  - `bills-support-oppose-count.csv`

```text
❌ BAD: parse CSV and count in the same function in main.py
✅ GOOD: readers → aggregates → report builders → writers
```
